{"output":"I’ll read the bug description and implementation, check the working tree, then fix it and run the existing tests.\n\nThe code starts every item at once, records completion order, and lets failures reject the whole call. I’ll use a bounded worker loop and capture each item’s failure. The shell startup also reported a configuration error; I’ll use a clean shell for verification.\n\nFixed concurrency limits, input-order results, limit validation, and per-item failure handling while preserving the documented API.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, an inline node --input-type=module contract probe, and git diff --check.\n\nOnly src/map.js and src/worker.js changed. No dependencies installed; no blockers.","final_output":"Fixed concurrency limits, input-order results, limit validation, and per-item failure handling while preserving the documented API.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, an inline node --input-type=module contract probe, and git diff --check.\n\nOnly src/map.js and src/worker.js changed. No dependencies installed; no blockers.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":7,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"error","action":"run","error":{"category":"command_failed","code":"nonzero_exit"},"command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short; ls -la AGENTS.md src/AGENTS.md tests/AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/queue-1-optimized/repo","exit_code":1,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":201,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-9a4c24db6c59190589352472cfe87f4b.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"grep_files","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test && node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { mapLimit } from './src/map.js';\nfor (const limit of [0, -1, 1.5, NaN, Infinity, '2', undefined, null]) {\n  await assert.rejects(mapLimit([1], limit, () => assert.fail('invalid limit launched work')), RangeError);\n  await assert.rejects(mapLimit([], limit, () => {}), RangeError);\n}\nlet active = 0, peak = 0;\nconst called = [];\nconst syncError = new Error('sync'), asyncError = new Error('async');\nconst results = await mapLimit([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 2, (item, index) => {\n  assert.equal(item, index);\n  called.push(index);\n  if (index === 1) throw syncError;\n  peak = Math.max(peak, ++active);\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => setTimeout(() => {\n    active--;\n    if (index === 2) reject(asyncError); else resolve(item * 2);\n  }, index === 0 ? 30 : 1));\n});\nassert.equal(peak, 2);\nassert.equal(active, 0);\nassert.deepEqual(called, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);\nassert.deepEqual(results, [\n  {status:'fulfilled', value:0}, {status:'rejected', reason:syncError},\n  {status:'rejected', reason:asyncError}, {status:'fulfilled', value:6},\n  {status:'fulfilled', value:8}\n]);\nassert.deepEqual(await mapLimit([1, 2], 10, x => x), [\n  {status:'fulfilled', value:1}, {status:'fulfilled', value:2}\n]);\nconsole.log('Contract probe passed');\nNODE\n git diff --check && git diff -- src/map.js src/worker.js && git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/queue-1-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":360,"stdout_bytes":1458,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-b3f0fb7e15b61529365a4edf74598286.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":39885,"output_tokens":1122},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":12160,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":12}}
